      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg daily, even with your confirmation. I can't verify the clinical context, and no indication I know of supports a dose five times the 10 mg maximum. An overdose could cause severe, prolonged hypotension and shock that is hard to reverse, so a general statement that the dose is intended isn't enough for me to place it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, and you can titrate from there.\n- **Pursue a nonstandard dose through pharmacy.** If you have a protocol or specialist recommendation behind 50 mg, discuss it with the pharmacist or attending first. If they approve, the order can be entered through their override process.\n- **Enter it with documentation.** If you give me the specific rationale, such as the protocol, the consulting service, or who approved it, I can include that in the order note. I'd still want pharmacy to verify before anything is given.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
